{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/924977-family-resemblance","id":924977,"title":"Family resemblance","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Beast: The Primordial"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-02T12:07:02-07:00","id":924977,"title":"Family resemblance","content":"Since a beast can only detect mages or psychics when they actively use this power, can beasts use family resemblance to ssense the uses of supernatural abilities? Or after the first detection they can no longer notice it.<br /> <br /> Also how about in regards to other supes they recognise on site?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1377-wrequis","name":"Wrequis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T13:03:19-07:00","id":924997,"title":"","content":"Yes, but only in so far as getting a general idea of what the other Supernatural is capable of and what they've most recently done. It's harder when detecting Fundamentally Human supernaturals, like Mages, Ghosts, and most all minor splats, but most supes are recognizable without rolling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Crunch isn't a hobby; it's a calling.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1959-hexmeister-vic","name":"Hexmeister Vic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1959_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"764"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T14:19:08-07:00","id":925042,"title":"","content":"Sorry what I'm asking is after a beast recognises a mage after he casts a spell, would he get that roll again later in the story when the mage is casting a spell, or if a changeling activates a contract in his proximity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1377-wrequis","name":"Wrequis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T15:35:10-07:00","id":925072,"title":"","content":"Wreq, a Beast still gets the check even if the individual hasn't used a supernatural power recently. Just that in the event that the target has not used a supernatural power in the same scene then the integrity (or nearest analogue) is added to the subtraction part of the check in addition to composure. <br /> <br /> Changelings are called out as automatically being detected when the Beast is in it's presence so long as it isn't using supernatural means to hide its nature in which case we get a clash on the check. Changelings aren't close enough to baseline human to get the protection of not having used a power in the scene making them harder to detect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T17:30:23-07:00","id":925128,"title":"","content":"But can a beast use this ability akin to a changelings kenning, or an unseen sense merit","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1377-wrequis","name":"Wrequis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T18:10:50-07:00","id":925143,"title":"","content":"I don't have Changeling ,yet, so I can't really compare there. (When I looked it up all I got was a talent and there are too many details in the description I don't fully understand to fairly make an assessment.)<br /> <br /> As for <i>Unseen Sense</i> well on a base <i> Family Resemblance</i> is stronger since the only supernatural beings it doesn't (at least potentially) trigger on are one's that are not actually in the material world. I'm going to presume you're inquiry is about whether or not resemblance has an equivalency to immediately pointing out X is a vampire by accepting a spooked condition once a chapter, correct? I ask since your initial post implies the idea of making the check repeatedly on the same target which strikes me as a little weird since it isn't like you're going to encounter a mage on Monday, then run into him Tuesday and if he doesn't trip mage again assume &quot;Oh he must not be a mage anymore.&quot; <br /> <br /> Or is this the scenario you're inquiring about?. You run into Tim the Enchanter on Monday and you succeed on the check (but not exceptionally) so you know Tim is mage that is running on fumes as far as magical power is going. Then you run into him on Tuesday and you want to make the check again to identify see if Tim has managed to refill his reserves or aim for the exceptional success and find out that his favored form of magic is probability manipulation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-02T18:14:05-07:00","id":925145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wrequis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/924977-family-resemblance?p=925128#post925128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But can a beast use this ability akin to a changelings kenning, or an unseen sense merit</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they cannot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T00:52:47-07:00","id":925259,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/924977-family-resemblance?p=925145#post925145\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, they cannot.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1377-wrequis","name":"Wrequis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T01:04:56-07:00","id":925260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/924977-family-resemblance?p=925143#post925143\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or is this the scenario you're inquiring about?. You run into Tim the Enchanter on Monday and you succeed on the check (but not exceptionally) so you know Tim is mage that is running on fumes as far as magical power is going. Then you run into him on Tuesday and you want to make the check again to identify see if Tim has managed to refill his reserves or aim for the exceptional success and find out that his favored form of magic is probability manipulation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> While that wasn't my original question, I do have another about this. if the roll is automatocally a success on vampires changelings sin-eaters, does that mean you always know how 'full' other supes are in your proximity?<br /> <br /> Also with the mage thing itd be weird to be besties with them, then one day get a dramatic failure because the increased their gnosis and all of a sudden they don't like you for staring :/","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1377-wrequis","name":"Wrequis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T01:27:43-07:00","id":925265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wrequis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/924977-family-resemblance?p=925260#post925260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> While that wasn't my original question, I do have another about this. if the roll is automatocally a success on vampires changelings sin-eaters, does that mean you always know how 'full' other supes are in your proximity?<br /> <br /> Also with the mage thing itd be weird to be besties with them, then one day get a dramatic failure because the increased their gnosis and all of a sudden they don't like you for staring :/</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't an auto success. It's triggered reflexively and a supernatural like a changeling, werewolf, or vampire, the ones that are basically another species, only receive their composure as a defense against being detected unless they're using another supernatural power to mask their nature. Only other Beasts are automatically known barring extra work to hide their nature. It's just that the difficulty isn't that high to my knowledge and the beast is going to be rolling wits+occult+lair with only the target's composure as a defense. So more often than not a Beast will be able to id the presence of another supernatural off the bat.<br /> <br /> As for repeated checks, the rules don't say you make one every time you end up in the presence of a specific supernatural after the first time. While I wouldn't say it wouldn't be amusing for a Beast to say have a guy they work with all the time and just do to horrible luck have never picked up on the fact that the dude is a werewolf and just have the reveal happen one day, I would say it would also be kind of an annoying move to say you have to do the check every time even after you've identified them.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T11:17:10-07:00","id":925418,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/924977-family-resemblance?p=925265#post925265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It isn't an auto success. It's triggered reflexively and a supernatural like a changeling, werewolf, or vampire, the ones that are basically another species, only receive their composure as a defense against being detected unless they're using another supernatural power to mask their nature. Only other Beasts are automatically known barring extra work to hide their nature. It's just that the difficulty isn't that high to my knowledge and the beast is going to be rolling wits+occult+lair with only the target's composure as a defense. So more often than not a Beast will be able to id the presence of another supernatural off the bat.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Detecting a vampire, werewolf, changeling, or other full-fledged supernatural being is relatively easy for a Beast and happens reflexively if the Beast is physically in their presence. Success is automatic unless the target is hiding her nature by supernatural means, in which case the Beast must win a Clash of Wills before using Family Resemblance. &quot; -page 88<br /> <br /> It does say that success is automatic","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1377-wrequis","name":"Wrequis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T11:39:48-07:00","id":925432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wrequis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/924977-family-resemblance?p=925418#post925418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Detecting a vampire, werewolf, changeling, or other full-fledged supernatural being is relatively easy for a Beast and happens reflexively if the Beast is physically in their presence. Success is automatic unless the target is hiding her nature by supernatural means, in which case the Beast must win a Clash of Wills before using Family Resemblance. &quot; -page 88<br /> <br /> It does say that success is automatic</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you're not getting a dramatic failure because you're not making a roll.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T12:32:35-07:00","id":925459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/924977-family-resemblance?p=925432#post925432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then you're not getting a dramatic failure because you're not making a roll.</div> </div> </div> </div>unless you still make the roll when you meet them, but treat a failure as a success. Meaning you have a chance of an exceptional success<br /> <br /> Also meaning a beast can always see how much fuel stat another true supe has at all times.<br /> <br /> Overall the wording on this ability is really confusing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1377-wrequis","name":"Wrequis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-03T13:33:16-07:00","id":925479,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wrequis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/924977-family-resemblance?p=925459#post925459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> unless you still make the roll when you meet them, but treat a failure as a success. Meaning you have a chance of an exceptional success<br /> <br /> Also meaning a beast can always see how much fuel stat another true supe has at all times.<br /> <br /> Overall the wording on this ability is really confusing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really, I think you're just over thinking things. If you're getting an automatic success you don't make a roll because there's no chance of failure. You don't get an exceptional success or failure. Yeah you might opt to make the roll regardless, but then what you're doing is trying to analyze the individual. That's why failure says you don't learn anything it's not &quot;you don't know the group are werewolves&quot; it's &quot; the group are werewolves, but you've got no clue on anything further than that.&quot; It's also why dramatic failure peeves them off your visibly staring and sizing them up as either an opponent or food. <br /> <br /> I'm also gonna say that a Beast isn't always aware of how much power the other has at all times since it only says that detecting those groups is easy. Sizing up their power level and mp bar are a bit more than just detecting them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}